read_head_oid and read_index_trailer re-derive two of the fingerprint's canonical signals — the HEAD oid, following one symref hop through the loose ref then packed-refs and yielding the 40-zero sentinel for an unborn HEAD, and the 20-byte SHA-1 trailer of .git/index — from small raw file reads with no gix open, because the gate runs on every invocation and must stay stat-cheap. The publish side derives the same two through gix, so each raw reader must reproduce gix's byte form exactly, sentinel included, or the gate can never hit.
